Subject: [PATCH 01/37] feat: add Pydantic Settings-based config package
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replaces the flat, unvalidated config.py with config/settings.py — a
pydantic-settings Settings model. Every field is validated at startup
(risk_percent must be a positive percentage, log_level must be a real
level, etc.) instead of failing silently deep in trading logic.

Values load from JQE_-prefixed env vars or a .env file, in addition to
documented defaults. get_settings() is an lru_cache-wrapped factory so
importing config never performs I/O as a side effect; config.settings
is a convenience alias to the same cached instance.

Adds .env.example documenting every supported variable.
